    "name": "Query Parameters",
    "responsibility": "Holds a command's parameters in a collection that exists without a command object, so a caller can build a parameter set on its own thread and hand the finished set to a data method. It also reads typed values back out of a parameter after execution, deciding for each .NET type whether a database null becomes a null, a sentinel value, or a refusal.",
